l recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[37,38],"#Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[39,41],"#Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[40,41],"#Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[42,44],"#Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[43,44],"#Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[45,46],"#Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[46,46]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/BB6V748H","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/6T2VT84L?page=1&annotation=RHX5TJ82","line":37},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/6T2VT84L?page=1&annotation=RL368296","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/6T2VT84L?page=2&annotation=I252AL4W","line":43},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/6T2VT84L?page=6&annotation=7V6FEREW","line":46}],"metadata":{"Title":"Evaluating reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT's nutritional recommendations for women with polycystic ovary syndrome","Authors":"Elif Ulug, Irmak Gunesli, Aylin Acıkgoz Pinar, Bulent Okan Yildiz","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1016/j.nutres.2024.11.005","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aims to evaluate the reliability, quality, and readability of ChatGPT’s responses to nutrition-related questions asked by women with PCOS","Findings":"Our results suggest that ChatGPT’s responses to nutrition-related questions about PCOS are generally of high quality, but improvements in both reliability and readability are still necessary.","Conclusions":"considered a substitute for personalized medical advice from health care professionals for effective management of the syndrome.","Limitations":"First, validated tools need to be developed to evaluate ChatGPT responses, which would eliminate heterogeneity in comparing the obtained data with the literature. Second, although there is consistency between the first and second answers received by ChatGPT and the reliability of these answers is high, there is no single correct answer to a questi","User_Notes":"promptlar ve yanıtlar var  klinisyen değ var karşılaştırma yok  ai klinisyen yerine geçmemeli denmiş"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1ijl1m1","at":1774939743098},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/ulugEvaluatingReliabilityQuality2025b.md"},
